{"key":"556b5070ccf0a096","source_file":"Potts Mi - My.json","source_id":20836,"source_url":"concordance-monstrous-ppl-immanis","term":"Monstrous","headwords":["Monstrous"],"latin":["Immanis"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Monstrous"],"latin":["Immanis"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE","TCR"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"1787","subsection":"3"},"text":"The Lord's temptations were the most monstrous (or frightful) of all.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"123","subsection":"end"},"text":"Hell is like a monstrous lion.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"488","subsection":null},"text":"The monstrous faith that...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"388","subsection":"9"},"text":"A monstrous lion () = the power of falsity from evil.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"403","subsection":"6"},"text":"By the teeth of a lion are signified the falsities of that evil; and, as these destroy all the truths and goods of the Church, they are called the teeth of a lion, and the molars of that monstrous lion ().","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"monstrous","url":"/meta/potts/monstrous/"}